<|start-latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|end-latent|>Visual 'FISHMANE' contradicts 'dweb.link' domain; hosted on an IPFS gateway (ipfs.dweb.link) to obscure origin and bypass filters; high URL entropy confirms obfuscation. Hash-like subdomain; IPFS hosting; credential theft focus; total brand/domain mismatch. Based on these signals, this webpage is classified as malicious. <answer>malicious</answer><|im_end|>
<|start-latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|latent|><|end-latent|>Risk level is high because the button facilitates the theft of user credentials; the sensitive operation is data_submission (password harvesting); deception indicators include the impersonation of a login page hosted on a decentralized infrastructure to bypass security filters; this matches the credential_harvesting malicious pattern. This button directly assists the malicious intent of the page by acting as the submission trigger for the stolen credentials; label: malicious — the button is the final step in a phishing flow hosted on a suspicious IPFS domain, designed to harvest user passwords. <answer>malicious</answer><|im_end|>

